e calories you'd  be surprised what cutting butter sugar a  bit of milk etc out of your diet can  achieve  likewise use less oil in your cooking  etc or use the strategy I outlined in my  book super functional training and eat  low calorie meals for breakfast and  lunch so that you can safely enjoy  yourself at dinner dinner tends to be  the most social meal and that means we  like to really enjoy it so this method  works really well for me the other key  to ripped abs though is to train your  core properly a lot of people will tell  you that getting great abs is only about  diet and this just isn't true while  losing fat will mean that your abs look  more visible through your midsection the  truth is that you also need to make them  stronger so that they push through more  don't believe me try contracting your  abs and looking in the mirror you'll see  that they look better that's because  you've flattened your stomach by  tightening your transverse abdominis and  protruded your six-pack by flexing your  rectus abdominis get stronger and your  abs will look closer to this all the  time this will also improve your posture  don't just train the front muscles for  flat abs you need to use exercises that  challenge you to brace your core one of  the best options for this is the hollow  body hold that you can also try plank  variations planche variations front  lever dragon flag LaLanne push-ups V ups  AB rollouts or uber vacuums  the other tip is to likewise train the  transverse plane a great midsection is  comprised of a six-pack but also defined  tube leaks on either side this gives you  that look of a shredded rippling  midsection rather than just a stuck on  set of abs combined with a low body fat  percentage it's a mean combo some great  options for this include harloff presses  medval throws heavy bag work cable punch  outs one-armed push-ups lizard crawls  and briefcase carries oh and when you do  train your rectus abdominis make sure  you're actually targeting the right area  many people will actually engage their  hip flexors rather than their abs when  doing sit-ups or crunches same with leg  raises  remember your abs are used to pull your  upper body towards your lower body focus  on crunching the core rolling it  forwards not folding at the waist I've  been doing a lot more of this kind of  training lately and that's played a big  role in giving me more defined abs  ultimately form follows function train  for performance and your looks will take  care of themselves something else I've  been doing a whole lot more up since  lockdown is walking seeing as my wife  and daughter weren't able to go to their  usual classes together during the day  we've been walking as a family in the  evenings which has been something really  nice to come out of all this walking is  a fantastic way of burning more calories  throughout the day in a very low  intensity manner and in fact if you want  to improve your general fitness one of  the best things you can do is to add  more extremely low intensity cardio to  your routine we're not supposed to be  either going full out all the time  or completely  we're supposed to be gently moving  constantly and this is something else  that I've been doing as well I made a  video recently a few months back about  splitting your workouts take a day and  incidental training so just finding ways  to get a small bursts of activity  throughout your day rather than just  relying on one big burst of exertion at  the gym for an hour or two hours and I  think this has also contributed a lot to  my general improvements in terms of  fitness and you know that more lean look  so it's something that I'm gonna keep  doing and I highly recommend to everyone  ultimately you shouldn't think of it as  training think of it as adaptation  change your environment and change your  routine and your body and your  performance will change in kind and  there you have it that's how I got more  ripped and that's what you need to do to  get more shredded abs hope you found  this useful and interesting let me know  how you train your midsection in the  comments down below and what you'd like  to hear about next give this video a  like and share it around if you enjoyed  it that helps me out immensely and of  course subscribe for much more like this  I've got lots more exciting stuff on the  way and if you want to learn more about  training for function first and  improving your general performance  you'll probably enjoy my ebook and  training programs super functional  training you can find a link to that in  the description down below and there's  discount on right now whilst we're all  in lockdown or some of us are anyways  thanks a ton for watching this one and  bye for now  so a few people had asked why I haven't  been doing these on camera talking  segments for a while okay one person  asked the reason I'm see was that my  hair was so awful that I just couldn't  do it but I'm coming back from the  hairdresser's now and I'm feeling a lot  more like myself so hi
 

